            "review_title": "Review at Quan Hoi Đo",
            "review_text": "Micke9\nHuntington Beach, California4 contributions\n0\nAuthentic Vietnamese Cuisine\nFeb 2017 • Business\nIf you have been to \"Cuc Gach\" restaurant in Saigon, you will like this restaurant. Authentic vietnamese cuisine in a setting of Vietnam in the 80s when things are simple. Table and chairs are intentionally crudely made and has worn out with time. The whole ambience brings you back to another world and another time far away. An ideal place to have lunch. Cool breeze in the shaded front yard without the need of air cond. Lunch is served like a typical lunch prepared by servants to an upper middle class Vietnam family in the 80s. Staff is really friendly and helpful. The food comes out quick and hot. Pumpkin soup is to die for. Fried \"Huong\" fish with green mango is the best. \"Ca kho to\" is also great. Have been back a few times for lunch. Get the table inside the house, it is the best table, very clean and give you a unique feeling like you are the owner of the house. My favorite place in Can Tho\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 5, 2017",
