            "review_text": "gungle11\nHanoi, Vietnam6 contributions\n0\nExcellent Vietnamese food\nJun 2016 • Friends\nI found this place when we came to my cousin house ( hem thoi trang ) I thought we should give it a try and it turned out more than we expected. The place is clean, modern and nice, we got there around 2:50 and found out the kitchen close at 4pm. So, we immediately put in our orders. \n Canh Ga Chien (Chicken wings) for appetizers\n Hu Tieu Kho\n Vietnamese Banana Cake\n Ice tea\nEverything is tasty except for the tea, which I can go without. While we were eating and the kitchen was closed, the kitchen staffs came out and have their lunch. To our delight, all of them are Vietnamese - no wonder the food was so good and authentic.\nThe service? The waiter we had was really courteous and nice. He made us feel relax and enjoy our meal even though the place is already closed for break between lunch and dinner. \nIf and when I am in the city and craving for Vietnamese food, I will definitely come here and try other dishes.\nRead more\nWritten June 14, 2016",
